cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "SuperdiffusionCLT: a Lean 4 formalization of the superdiffusive central limit theorem for a Brownian particle in a critically-correlated incompressible random drift"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper of Armstrong, Bou-Rabee and Kuusi on a
  Brownian particle in a critically-correlated incompressible random drift: the quenched superdiffusive
  invariance principle (Theorem A), quantitative homogenization (Theorem B), the large-scale C^{0,γ} and
  C^{1,γ} estimates (Theorems C and D), and the asymptotics of the renormalized diffusivities, built on the
  public CoarseGraining homogenization library and the public MarkovProcess library. The library contains
  no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - superdiffusion
  - stochastic homogenization
  - central limit theorem
